A||||5||mshill||Acquired major hatchet job today...||||1||
Z||000000||mshill||10-16-2000||01:20 AM||||Today I towed home an 85SE Fiero that I was going to buy from a guy.  Instead I ended up buying a set of turbo rims with new tires for $200 and he threw in the car.  The body is pretty straight except for a crack in the roof just at the top of the pillar.  And thats where the good news stops.<P>He opens the trunk (with a screw driver cause the lockset is missing) and gues what kind of motor I find... a 2.8L from on of those Pontiac 6000 series cars.  Yup, the intake went off in the wrong direction and had ugly blue valve covers and the coid was mounted sideways up where it has no business being. Of course the EGR stuff is all whacked and it had some little shock absorber instead of a dogbone.  OOOOHHHH, THE HUMANITY.<P>So I towed it home and told my 14 yr old son that the car is his, but he has to buy the tires and wheels from me.  The good news is that I have a line on a cradle with a V6 and auto tranny on it that I will just drop into it to get rid of that backward V6 engine.<P>Good thing it's two years before he can drive, cause I got a feeling it's going to take us that long to fix it up.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||10-16-2000||10:59 AM||||I had understood that the top of the intake can be reversed by just unbolting it and turning it around. I realise even if that's the case it doesn't solve everything but it might be worth trying before you yank the engine.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||10-16-2000||11:13 AM||||I've seen a V6 plenium off before and I think 2 of the 8 intake passages blocked off because it only needs 6 of them?  I'd imagine putting the plenium on backwards or the intake manifold would leave only 4 intake passages open to the cylinders wouldn't it?  What I'm thinking is, the way it is right now probably is making a V4?<P>I've seen a 6000 swap and it changed nothing with the intake setup.  I think you should be able to fix the problem just by turning the intake back around.<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">            <BR>   <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A>  <p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 10-16-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000003||mshill||10-16-2000||11:48 AM||||Ogre, Tigger,<P>There is so much more wrong with this thing that it will actually be less work to drop the whole cradle and stuff one in there that I know has been taken care of.  Looks like TerryK is going to give me a complete V6 auto on a cradle with wiring harness intact.  Thanks Terry.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tigger||10-16-2000||01:12 PM||||Yep, that's probably the route I would take too, especially if the engine harness is hacked (mine was so bad, can't believe it ran after comparing it to the good one when I had it out of the car).<P>Anyway, I just wanted to let you know that the engine will work in a Fiero and maybe something to keep around and rebuild to have as a backup engine.  Sounds like fun, good luck with it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||mshill||10-16-2000||03:05 PM||||Tigger,  thanks for the note.  I am getting my 3.4L pushrod engine this week for my "currently in progress" project car (as opposed to this mutant I picked up yesterday) so I will have two V6 blocks laying around when I am done.  I will likely dump most of the 6000 engine and save the cradle and auto tranny for a buildup some time in the future.  I have two more sons that will eventually need cars (Fieros) an a couple of years.<BR>||||reg||1
